D. the comparison constants as the index falls towards 2 from above.
   Radial moments in closed form (E R^p = a/(a-p)); only E||Z||^{-theta} is
   Monte Carlo.  E R^2 has infinite variance below index 4, so estimating it
   gave 7.87 and 27.17 on two runs at index 2.2 where the exact value is 11.
        index  E R^2 exact    c(0.0)    c(0.5)    c(1.0)    c(1.5)    c(2.0)   min d_*
          2.2        11.00     1.000     0.278     0.163     0.120     0.100    0.4019
          2.5         5.00     1.000     0.486     0.326     0.255     0.220    0.4019
          3.0         3.00     1.000     0.648     0.490     0.408     0.366    0.4019
          6.0         1.50     1.000     0.864     0.783     0.742     0.732    0.4019
   d_* stays bounded away from zero (min 0.4019); c(theta)
   collapses towards zero as the index falls to 2: yes (E R^2 is its denominator).
   So the comparison degrades through its CONSTANT, not through the shrinkage
   factors, and at index 2 it stops existing because K does.
   -> [ok]

